====================================================================================================
READING IT
====================================================================================================
   fitted   eps ~ T_total^(-0.217)

   SQL / arXiv:2606.19486  Theta(Lambda/eps^2)  ->  slope -0.500
   Heisenberg-limited      O(1/eps)             ->  slope -1.000

   WORSE THAN SQL. twirl_cal does not reach the control-free optimum on
   its own axis, so the O(1) circuit count is the only claim it can make.

   Against Huang et al.'s O(1/eps) for KNOWN structure - twirl_cal's actual
   problem class - anything at SQL is a full factor of 1/eps behind.

  Scope: N=3, M=9, one coefficient draw, noiseless, 3 seeds, 13 points
  spanning several decades of T_total. A slope fitted over that range is
  indicative, not a scaling law; the bias floor at large T bends it.
